{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_101","type":"agent_message","text":"The corruption is now explained by an actual C behavior: for the BLAKE backend, `SPX_gen_message_random` writes the full BLAKE digest (32 or 64 bytes) even though `SPX_N` is smaller. The normal signer has enough trailing signature space, so this is intentional ground-truth behavior for the translation. I’m updating the Rust export and tests to reproduce that exact over-wide write."}}
